
### Request 1 saves the new listing's id; later requests reuse it as {{listingId}}.
@base = http://localhost:8080/api

############################ SUCCESS ############################

### 1. Host creates a listing  -> 201
POST {{base}}/host/listings
X-Host-Id: host-1
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Beach House", "description": "Sea view", "pricePerNight": 100}

> {% client.global.set("listingId", response.body.id); %}

### 2. Anyone browses listings (no header)  -> 200
GET {{base}}/listings

### 3. Anyone views one listing  -> 200
GET {{base}}/listings/{{listingId}}

### 4. Host views their own listings  -> 200
GET {{base}}/host/listings
X-Host-Id: host-1

### 5. Host updates their listing  -> 200
PUT {{base}}/host/listings/{{listingId}}
X-Host-Id: host-1
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Beach House", "description": "Renovated", "pricePerNight": 120}

### 6. Guest books 3 nights  -> 201, totalPrice = 3 x 120 = 360.00
POST {{base}}/bookings
X-Guest-Id: guest-1
Content-Type: application/json

{"listingId": {{listingId}}, "startDate": "2026-12-01", "endDate": "2026-12-04"}

### 7. Guest views their bookings  -> 200
GET {{base}}/bookings
X-Guest-Id: guest-1

### 8. Host views bookings on their listings  -> 200
GET {{base}}/host/bookings
X-Host-Id: host-1

########################### BUSINESS RULES ###########################

### R1. Overlapping dates (Dec 3-5 overlaps Dec 1-4)  -> 409
POST {{base}}/bookings
X-Guest-Id: guest-2
Content-Type: application/json

{"listingId": {{listingId}}, "startDate": "2026-12-03", "endDate": "2026-12-05"}

### R2. Back-to-back is allowed (check in on Dec 4, the day guest-1 checks out)  -> 201
POST {{base}}/bookings
X-Guest-Id: guest-2
Content-Type: application/json

{"listingId": {{listingId}}, "startDate": "2026-12-04", "endDate": "2026-12-05"}

### R3. Host cannot book their own listing  -> 400
POST {{base}}/bookings
X-Guest-Id: host-1
Content-Type: application/json

{"listingId": {{listingId}}, "startDate": "2027-01-10", "endDate": "2027-01-12"}

### R4. Start date in the past  -> 400
POST {{base}}/bookings
X-Guest-Id: guest-2
Content-Type: application/json

{"listingId": {{listingId}}, "startDate": "2020-01-01", "endDate": "2020-01-03"}

### R5. End date not after start date  -> 400
POST {{base}}/bookings
X-Guest-Id: guest-2
Content-Type: application/json

{"listingId": {{listingId}}, "startDate": "2027-01-10", "endDate": "2027-01-10"}

### R6. Booking a listing that doesn't exist  -> 404
POST {{base}}/bookings
X-Guest-Id: guest-2
Content-Type: application/json

{"listingId": 999999, "startDate": "2027-01-10", "endDate": "2027-01-12"}

### R7. Another host tries to update host-1's listing  -> 404
PUT {{base}}/host/listings/{{listingId}}
X-Host-Id: host-2
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Hijacked", "pricePerNight": 1}

### R8. Listing without a title  -> 400
POST {{base}}/host/listings
X-Host-Id: host-1
Content-Type: application/json

{"pricePerNight": 50}

### R9. Price must be > 0  -> 400
POST {{base}}/host/listings
X-Host-Id: host-1
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Free room", "pricePerNight": 0}

### R10. Missing identity header  -> 401
GET {{base}}/bookings

### R11. Malformed JSON / bad date format / non-numeric id  -> 400
POST {{base}}/bookings
X-Guest-Id: guest-2
Content-Type: application/json

{"listingId": {{listingId}}, "startDate": "01/12/2026", "endDate": "2026-12-05"}

### R12. Non-numeric id in the path  -> 400
GET {{base}}/listings/abc
